    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/hawaiiedu/jobs/5477357/administrative-services-manager-director-of-aloha-intelligence-institute-0096": {
      "title": "Administrative Services Manager (Director of Aloha Intelligence Institute) (#0096984T)",
      "description": "Career Opportunities at the University of Hawai'i | University of Hawai'i For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Administrative Services Manager (Director of Aloha Intelligence Institute) (#0096984T) | University of Hawai'i page has loaded. Administrative Services Manager (Director of Aloha Intelligence Institute) (#0096984T) | University of Hawai'i page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Career Opportunities at the University of Hawai'i Menu Career Opportunities at the University of Hawai'i Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. University of Hawai'i powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Administrative Services Manager (Director of Aloha Intelligence Institute) (#0096984T) Print Apply ﻿ Administrative Services Manager (Director of Aloha Intelligence Institute) (#0096984T) Salary See Position Description Location UH System Offices, Honolulu, HI Job Type Full-Time Temporary Job Number 2026-01951 Department Office of the Vice President for Research and Innovation System Opening Date 09/09/2026 Closing Date 10/9/2026 11:59 PM Hawaii Position Number: 96984T Description Title: Administrative Services Manager (Director of Aloha Intelligence Institute) Position Number: 0096984T Hiring Unit: Office of the Vice President for Research and Innovation (OVPRI) Location: UH System Sinclair Building Date Posted: September 9, 2026 Closing Date: October 9, 2026 Band: D Salary: salary schedules and placement information Additional salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Temporary/Permanent: Temporary Other Conditions: This position is annually renewable contingent upon satisfactory performance and/or availability of funding. The Aloha Intelligence Institute is envisioned as a statewide, community-grounded artificial intelligence institute designed to serve the University of Hawai'i System and the people, agencies, businesses, and communities of Hawai'i through shared AI infrastructure, coordinated expertise, interdisciplinary applied research, responsible governance, workforce development, and an applied service model. The Institute is intended to operate as a UH systemwide hub for ethical, place-based, and human-centered AI that supports public benefit, community needs, environmental resilience, local innovation, and practical adoption across sectors. Duties and Responsibilities (NOTE: ** denotes Essential Functions) **Provides administrative oversight to the launch and initial operationalization of the Aloha Intelligence Institute as a statewide, community-grounded AI initiative, under the direction of the Vice President for Research and Innovation. **Responsible for implementing the establishment of the organizational and administrative framework for the Institute, including launch governance, advisory structures, working groups, affiliate pathways, and internal coordination mechanisms. **Oversees development of the Institute’s phased project pipeline, including early landscape scans, roadmap development, partner intake, pilot identification, and launch of selected applied projects. **Coordinates landscape scans and partner consultations to identify statewide opportunities, capacity gaps, responsible use cases, and priority domains for institute action. **Directs preparation of early roadmaps and implementation frameworks across domains such as education, health, climate and resilience, government services, culture and language, and business innovation as appropriate. **Coordinates the early design of shared institute cores and applied labs, including technical infrastructure, responsible AI governance, community partnerships, translation support, workforce pathways, evaluation support, and innovation/commercialization coordination. **Helps promote responsible, human-centered, place-based AI consistent with UH values and the Institute’s commitment to public benefit, fairness, transparency, cultural integrity, and community engagement. **Coordinates use of initial institute space, collaboration environments, and systemwide facilities that support research, teaching, prototyping, convening, and partner engagement. **Translates the Institute’s mission into executable initiatives that support applied research, service delivery, workforce development, and responsible AI capability-building across Hawai'i. **Builds and coordinates cross-campus, cross-disciplinary, and cross-sector collaborations involving UH campuses, system offices, state and county agencies, schools, community organizations, non-profits, cultural organizations, and industry partners. **Coordinates with UH academic units, community colleges, system offices, and external stakeholders to connect institute activities with internships, capstones, applied projects, workshops, and workforce pathways. **Works with faculty, technical personnel, students, and partners to stand up pilot-ready project pathways that move ideas into structured evaluation, prototyping, and testing. **Works with UH academic, policy, legal, cultural, and community experts to ensure appropriate treatment of Indigenous, cultural, environmental, health, agency, and community-sensitive data and knowledge. **Coordinates with relevant UH offices on operational requirements related to personnel, facilities, technology support, communications, contracts, agreements, and other startup matters consistent with University procedures. **Identifies opportunities to align the Institute with UH strategic priorities, federal and state opportunities, community needs, and innovation and commercialization pathways. **Ensures that projects are assessed not only for technical feasibility, but also for public benefit, fairness, sustainability, cultural integrity, community alignment, and responsible data use. Other duties as assigned. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Education and Professional Experience Possession of a baccalaureate degree in business, management, or a related field and seven (7) years of progressively responsible professional experience with responsibilities in leadership experience in a university, research institute, public-sector innovation environment, technology initiative, or similarly complex organization; or any equivalent combination of education and/or professional work experience which provides the required education, knowledge, skills and abilities as indicated. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Extensive knowledge of innovative and state-of-the-art principles, concepts, emerging theories, the current federal and state laws and associated rules, regulations and interpretations and systems associated with leadership experience in a university, research institute, public-sector innovation environment, technology initiative, or similarly complex organization. Demonstrated ability to develop short- and long-term plans of actions, understand problems from a broad perspective, use creative reasoning to discern broad underlying principles and issues when problem solving. Demonstrated written and verbal mastery in presenting ideas, theories, issues and models clearly and accurately using persuasion and negotiation to build consensus and cooperation and provide long-term direction and leadership. Demonstrated ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with internal and external organizations, groups and individuals. Demonstrated ability to operate a personal computer and apply word processing software. For supervisory work, demonstrated ability to lead subordinates, manage work priorities and projects, and manage employee relations. SUPPLEMENTAL MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Demonstrated experience of a substantial record of managing complex initiatives, cross-functional teams, or partnerships at the intersection of AI and business or public-sector organizations. Demonstrated experience launching, building, or scaling a major initiative, center, institute, program, or cross-organizational effort. Demonstrated substantive knowledge of artificial intelligence to assess technical claims, recognize limitations and risks, lead interdisciplinary institute development, and build effective partnerships with government, industry, and community organizations. Demonstrated experience in strategic planning, program development, partnership-building, and implementation management. Demonstrated commitment to ethical, responsible, and community-informed approaches to innovation and technology deployment. Demonstrated ability to focus on artificial intelligence, data-driven decision-making, digital innovation, or technology-intensive enterprises. DESIRABLE QUALIFICATIONS Master’s degree (MBA or equivalent) in business, management, or a related field, preferably with demonstrated focus on artificial intelligence, data-driven decision-making, digital innovation, or technology-intensive enterprises. Experience working in or with higher education systems, statewide initiatives, or multi-campus environments. Experience working with Hawai'i-based communities, agencies, cultural organizations, or public-sector partners. Experience in responsible AI, technology governance, data stewardship, digital policy, or community-engaged innovation. Experience developing external partnerships, affiliates, or collaborative program frameworks. Experience with interdisciplinary research development, applied innovation, commercialization pathways, or workforce development initiatives. Experience securing or positioning programs for external funding, public investment, philanthropy, or sponsored collaborations. Knowledge of issues related to Indigenous data governance, cultural stewardship, public benefit technology, or place-based innovation. To Apply: Select the \"Apply\" button in the top right corner of the screen; first-time NeoGov users will need to create an account. Please ensure your application includes the following materials: Cover Letter: A letter detailing your interest and how you meet both the minimum and desirable qualifications. All minimum qualifications must be met by the closing date to be considered. Resume/CV: A current professional resume or curriculum vitae. Professional References: The names, telephone numbers, and email addresses of three (3) professional references. Unofficial Transcripts: Copies of unofficial transcripts are required for the application, though official versions must be provided upon hire. Please note that copies of diplomas and academic summaries are not acceptable substitutes. Foreign Credential Evaluation: For degrees earned outside the U.S., you must provide a course-by-course analysis and equivalency statement from a NACES-member agency at your own expense. Important Note: To protect your privacy, do not include any photos, Social Security Numbers, or dates of birth in your packet. Only the most recent application will be reviewed, and all submitted materials become the property of the University of Hawai’i. Please ensure all documents are complete and legible to be considered by the search committee. Incomplete applications will not be considered. Inquiries: Chad Walton, Interim Vice President for Research and Innovation; cwalton@hawaii.edu EEO, Clery Act, ADA The University of Hawai'i is an Equal Opportunity Institution and is committed to a policy of nondiscrimination in employment, including on the basis of veteran and disability status.  For more information, visit: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/policies/ Employment is contingent on satisfying employment eligibility verification requirements of the Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986; reference checks of previous employers; and for certain positions, criminal history record checks. In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, annual campus crime statistics for the University of Hawai'i may be viewed at: https://www.hawaii.edu/titleix/help/campus-security/ , or a paper copy may be obtained upon request from the respective UH Campus Security or Administrative Services Office. In accordance with Article 10 of the unit 08 collective bargaining agreement, bargaining unit members receive priority consideration for APT job vacancies. As a result, external or non BU 08 applicants may not be considered for some APT vacancies. BU 08 members with re-employment rights or priority status are responsible for informing the hiring unit of their status. Accommodation Request: The University of Hawai'i complies with the provisions of the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). Applicants requiring a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process should contact the EEO coordinator directly. Determination on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis. For further information, please refer to the following link: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/accommodation-request/ Employer University of Hawaii Website http://workatuh.hawaii.edu Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Career Opportunities at the University of Hawai'i Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this setting does not apply, however, you can review your right on our privacy policy . If you require further assistance, please email privacy@neogov.com × Accessibility Statement At Governmentjobs.com, Inc. d/b/a NEOGOV, we recognize the importance of making our products\n                    and services accessible to all individuals, including those with disabilities, and are continually\n                    working to improve the experience for all users. Commitment to Accessibility We are committed to following best practices, including the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines\n                    (WCAG) 2.1, Level AA, to the extent feasible, however, we do not warrant compliance with these\n                    standards or any other accessibility standards. We are continually enhancing our platforms to\n                    ensure greater accessibility, and we actively seek out opportunities to improve accessibility features. Ongoing Enhancements Accessibility is an ongoing effort, and we are regularly updating our technology, services, and content\n                    to address accessibility barriers. Our team is dedicated to identifying areas for improvement and\n                    making enhancements that allow all users, regardless of their abilities, to fully engage with our\n                    services. Feedback and Assistance We value feedback from our users. If you encounter any accessibility barriers while using our services\n                    or have suggestions on how we can improve, please reach out to us at accessibility@neogov.com.\n                    We will make every effort to resolve any concerns and consider alternative options where possible. Thank you for choosing NEOGOV. We remain dedicated to improving accessibility and creating an\n                    inclusive experience for all. University of Hawai'i Career Opportunities at the University of Hawai'i Menu Close Menu University of Hawai'i Career Opportunities at the University of Hawai'i Civil Service Positions (Internal Applicants Only) Job Interest Card About UH Benefits University of Hawai'i's System Office of Human Resources Annual Campus Crime Stats Employment Related Posters/Brochures Help & Support Translate Support Job Application Job Details Applying as: | Support Close Close Cancel Clear SIGN Save We've updated our Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. Please, read and accept changes. Effective date: August 19, 2025 NEOGOV PRIVACY POLICY Contents 1. Introduction; Scope of this Policy. 2. Where We Are a Service Provider. 3. Personal Data We Collect About You and Why. 4. Cookies and Similar Tracking Technologies. 5. Online Analytics and Advertising. 6. Information We Disclose. 7. International Users. 8. Your Data Rights and Choices. 9. Notice to California Residents. 10. Your Rights and Control under EU GDPR. 11. Data Security and Integrity. 12. Retention and Removal. 13. Right to Revise. 14. Contact Details. 15. Privacy Contacts. Introduction; Scope of this Policy. The purpose of this Privacy Policy (the “Policy”) is to describe how we collect, use, store, protect, and disclose personal data online and offline either via our websites or related applications. This Policy applies to personal data we collect or use, and applications owned or controlled by Governmentjobs.com, Inc. (DBA “NEOGOV”), including our related brands NEOGOV.com, NEOED.com, PowerDMS.com, Governmentjobs.com, Schooljobs.com, and our mobile app(s) (collectively referred to as the “Services”), or affiliated companies (collectively referred to herein as “Governmentjobs”, \"Schooljobs\", “NEOGOV”, “NEOED”, “PowerDMS”, “we”, “us”, or “our”). By using any part of the Services you agree that you have read this Policy, your personal data will be processed as described herein, and you agree to be bound by this Policy. This Policy is incorporated into our Terms of Use . Definitions not explicitly defined herein shall retain the meaning as prescribed in the Terms of Use . Any dispute related to privacy is subject to the Terms of Use and this Policy, including limitations on liability. This Policy does not apply to (1) personal data controlled by our Customers (employers that utilize our Services, described further below), which is governed by our separate agreements and related data processing agreements with such Customers; (2) personal data collected by unaffiliated sites that link to or are accessible from our Services; (3) personal data our partners may collect directly from you and control; (4) personal data collected and processed by us about our employees or job applicants responding to our job offers; and, (5) non-personal data derived from personal data, including any data that is aggregated, de-identified, or anonymized, statistical data, insights, or other predictive data that is sufficiently different from your personal data that it cannot be reversed engineered through reasonable means, or otherwise identified from analysis or further processing of the derived data (collectively referred to as the “De-Identified Platform Data”). We use De-Identified Platform Data to provide Customers with useful and relevant insights, build features and data services, and improve our Services.  Because De-Identified Platform Data does not identify you personally, we can use and disclose it in our discretion. We are the controller for the personal data discussed in this Policy, except as noted in the “Where We Are"
