    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/hawaiiedu/jobs/5477361/interim-associate-director-casual": {
      "title": "Interim Associate Director (Casual)",
      "description": "Career Opportunities at the University of Hawai'i | University of Hawai'i For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Interim Associate Director (Casual) | University of Hawai'i page has loaded. Interim Associate Director (Casual) | University of Hawai'i page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Career Opportunities at the University of Hawai'i Menu Career Opportunities at the University of Hawai'i Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. University of Hawai'i powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Interim Associate Director (Casual) Print ﻿ Interim Associate Director (Casual) Salary See Position Description Location UH Manoa, Honolulu, HI Job Type Part-Time Temporary Job Number CASUAL Department University of Hawai'i at Manoa - CALL - Center for Philippine Studies Opening Date 09/09/2026 Closing Date 9/18/2026 11:59 PM Hawaii Position Number: CASUAL Description Title: Interim Associate Director (Casual) Position Number: Casual Hire Hiring Unit: College of Arts, Languages & Letters, Center for Philippine Studies Location: University of Hawaii at Manoa Date Posted: September 09, 2026 Closing Date: September 18, 2026 Salary: Minimum $26.69/hour, depending on qualifications and experience Full Time/Part Time: Up to 35 hours per week Temporary/Permanent: Temporary ***Applicants seeking short-term or part-time work with the University of Hawai‘i may apply for Casual Hire positions, which include administrative, professional, and technical (APT) or instructional-type positions. Because of the temporary nature of these appointments, Casual Hire employees are not eligible for most benefits provided to regular Board of Regents (BOR) and Civil Service employees (i.e. paid holidays/leave). Casual Hire appointments may last for up to 89 days for full-time employees, and up to 1 calendar year for part-time employees. Duties and Responsibilities * Assists the Director in strategic planning and implementing activities aligned with Center goals and university policies. *Coordinates and resolves operational and administrative matters in accordance with current policies, procedures, and directives. *Manages administrative and financial operations for instruction, research, and outreach initiatives, including program planning and public communications. *Assists in relaying general information on Philippine Studies-related coursework, scholarships, language programs, and overseas study opportunities. *Oversees Center communications, digital outreach, and information dissemination.  Executes the development and maintenance of the newsletter, listserv, and social media. *Designs and maintains databases of faculty, courses, and program activities. *Supports professional development opportunities *Plans and executes professional events, such as seminars, workshops, symposia, and conferences; supports communication endeavors of the Center, which may occur after business hours and/or on weekends. *Collaborates with internal and external stakeholders, including university faculty, students, alumni, public agencies, and key community and diplomatic organizations (e.g., the Philippine Consulate General in Honolulu and the Filipino Community Center), to drive the Center’s mission and objectives. *Attends relevant local, national, and international meetings to promote CPS activities and interact with other educational, program, and outreach coordinators. *Keeps abreast of University, State, and Federal rules, practices, and policies which are applicable to the CPS’s academic,  research, and outreach endeavors. *Works closely with the Director(s) of the Center for Philippine Studies and supervises students, graduate assistants, and other staff. Assists in language translation of communications and educational materials through the use of technology or other means. Performs other duties as assigned. *Denotes Essential Functions Minimum Qualifications Possession of a baccalaureate degree in Arts and Sciences, Education, Business Administration or related field and three (3) years of professional experience with responsibilities for program and administrative management; or any equivalent experience and training. Demonstrated capacity to carry out responsibilities involving fiscal administration and matters dealing with confidentiality. Demonstrated ability to plan, organize, and market events and programs, and carry out communication endeavors in both print and online media. Demonstrated ability to leverage technology as a tool for developing and maintaining administrative, planning, programmatic management (i.e. databases, spreadsheets), and communication systems (i.e.newsletter, listserv, social media). Demonstrated ability to work with individuals with diverse demographic populations and cultures in a multicultural environment. Possession of strong interpersonal, communication, and organizational skills. Ability to work nights and weekends, and travel to meetings and program-related events. Desirable Qualifications Advanced degree in Asian Studies, Philippine Studies, Philippine Languages, Ethnic Studies, American Studies, Education, Communications, Public Administration, Business Administration or related field. Beginner or other functional competence in Philippine languages. Considerable knowledge and experience with Philippine cultures and/or Filipino diasporic communities. Particular knowledge and/or experience in preparing grant applications and grant reports concerning the U.S. Title VI funding or other federal, private, or state agencies. Experience traveling and/or living in the Philippines or in the Filipino diasporic community. Familiarity with Native Hawaiian, Asian, and Pacific regional localities, drawing upon travel, residence, or academic studies. Demonstrated ability to work in a multicultural environment involving international connections, particularly with regards to Hawai?i, Asia, and the Pacific. Experience in working with administrative operations, policies, procedures, and laws involved in higher education or government. Familiarity with university policies, strategic goals, and core values. Familiarity with University of Hawai?i financial management systems. To Apply: Please submit the following materials by email attachment to Patricia Halagao, phalagao@hawaii.edu . A cover letter indicating how you satisfy the minimum and desirable qualifications Current resume Names of three (3) professional references (including phone number and e-mail addresses) Official transcripts (copies acceptable for application, but if selected, originals required upon hire) Inquiries: Patricia Halagao phalagao@hawaii.edu EEO, Clery Act, ADA The University of Hawai'i is an Equal Opportunity Institution and is committed to a policy of nondiscrimination in employment, including on the basis of veteran and disability status.  For more information, visit: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/policies/ Employment is contingent on satisfying employment eligibility verification requirements of the Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986; reference checks of previous employers; and for certain positions, criminal history record checks. In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, annual campus crime statistics for the University of Hawai'i may be viewed at: https://www.hawaii.edu/titleix/help/campus-security/ , or a paper copy may be obtained upon request from the respective UH Campus Security or Administrative Services Office. Accommodation Request: The University of Hawai'i complies with the provisions of the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). Applicants requiring a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process should contact the EEO coordinator directly. Determination on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis. For further information, please refer to the following link: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/accommodation-request/ Employer University of Hawaii Website http://workatuh.hawaii.edu Please verify your email address Verify Email Career Opportunities at the University of Hawai'i Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this setting does not apply, however, you can review your right on our privacy policy . If you require further assistance, please email privacy@neogov.com × Accessibility Statement At Governmentjobs.com, Inc. d/b/a NEOGOV, we recognize the importance of making our products\n                    and services accessible to