    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/hawaiiedu/jobs/5469339/public-information-specialist-events-coordinator-pos-0080444": {
      "title": "Public Information Specialist (Events Coordinator) (pos #0080444)",
      "description": "Career Opportunities at the University of Hawai'i | University of Hawai'i For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Public Information Specialist (Events Coordinator) (pos #0080444) | University of Hawai'i page has loaded. Public Information Specialist (Events Coordinator) (pos #0080444) | University of Hawai'i page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Career Opportunities at the University of Hawai'i Menu Career Opportunities at the University of Hawai'i Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. University of Hawai'i powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Public Information Specialist (Events Coordinator) (pos #0080444) Print Apply ﻿ Public Information Specialist (Events Coordinator) (pos #0080444) Salary See Position Description Location UH Hilo, Hilo, HI Job Type Full-Time Permanent Job Number 2026-01917 Department University of Hawai'i at Hilo Division University Relations Opening Date 09/03/2026 Closing Date 9/18/2026 11:59 PM Hawaii Position Number: 0080444 Description Title: Public Information Specialist (Events Coordinator) Position Number: 0080444 Hiring Unit: UH AT HILO, CHANCELLOR UHH, UNIVERSITY RELATIONS Location: UH at Hilo Date Posted: September 3, 2026 Closing Date: September 18, 2026 Band: B Salary : salary schedules and placement information Full Time/Part Time: Full-time Month: 11-month Temporary/Permanent: Permanent Other Conditions: Appointment to begin approximately October 2026, pending position clearance and availability of funding. Overview: The University of Hawai'i at Hilo (UH Hilo) is a public liberal arts and sciences university on the Island of Hawai'i, recognized for its integration of cultural immersion and place-based research that leverages the island's extraordinary geological, biological, and cultural diversity. A comprehensive, regional campus within the ten-campus University of Hawai'i system, UH Hilo offers high-quality undergraduate and select postgraduate education, with distinctive strengths in areas such as marine science, geology, astronomy, and Hawaiian language revitalization, while advancing research, scholarship, and creative activity that support community needs, environmental stewardship, Indigenous knowledge systems, and workforce development priorities for the State of Hawai'i. University Relations (UR) serves as the strategic communications, external engagement, and community relations arm of UH Hilo, advancing the institution's mission, visibility, and reputation through integrated marketing and communications, media relations, government relations, graphic services, web services, and institutional events. The unit supports enrollment, fundraising, community engagement, and institutional advancement goals by telling the UH Hilo story to diverse audiences across local, national, and international platforms. The Events Coordinator provides strategic leadership for institutional events across five major areas of responsibility: strategic events planning and development; budget and procurement; cross-departmental coordination and leadership; assessment and reporting; and community engagement and UR coordination. This position oversees the full lifecycle of institutional events at varying levels of service, from Chancellor's events to committee-driven campus activities, and supervises the Events Specialist. Duties and Responsibilities (* denotes essential functions): * Leads the strategic planning, development and execution of institutional events at varying levels of service, including full-service coordination for Chancellor's events. * Leads planning with cross-departmental support for signature annual events, including, but not limited to, commencement, homecoming, and alumni engagement activities. * Serves as lead point of contact for UH System events hosted at UH Hilo; and provides consultation and logistics support for committee-driven campus events. * Advances the strategic role of events as essential tools for community engagement, external relations, and institutional advancement; develops and implements creative event concepts that align with institutional priorities, reinforces the UH Hilo brand, and supports the goals of the UH Hilo Integrated Marketing and Communications Plan. * Serves as the primary point of contact for event planning, facility use, and campus space availability across campus departments, divisions and external organizations to ensure cohesive, high-quality events. * Establishes and maintains institutional event standards, protocols and best practices, including ceremonial procedures and protocol guidance for official university functions, in conjunction with the Director of Native Hawaiian Engagement. * Develops and maintains a comprehensive institutional events calendar and management system in coordination with campus departments and stakeholders. * Develops, manages, and monitors event budgets; advocates with institutional leadership for justified funding and resources necessary to execute quality events while ensuring efficient stewardship of allocated funds, fiscal accountability, and alignment with UH procurement policies. * Tracks and reconciles event expenditures, providing regular financial reports to UR leadership and identify opportunities for cost efficiencies. * Leads the development of policies, procedures, and informational materials related to external facility use, including future fee-based rental services as directed by institutional leadership. * Supervises and coordinates work direction to the Events Specialist, cross-departmental teams of 20-40+ contributors, volunteers and student assistants in the planning and execution of large-scale events. * Operationalizes executive leadership directives regarding campus-wide participation, commitment and contribution to institutional events with coordination of colleges, divisions and departments to ensure clarity of roles, expectations, and engagement requirements. * Develops and implements event-specific performance indicators and assessment process aligned with institutional goals and UH Hilo Integrated Marketing and Communications Plan, including attendance tracking, participant feedback and outcome measurements that indicate the effectiveness and inform continuous improvement. Navigates university procurement processes to secure vendors, services, equipment and supplies involving the accurate management of contracts, purchase orders and reimbursements in coordination with UR administrative and fiscal support staff. Builds and maintains relationships with community organizations, businesses, and nonprofits to position UH Hilo as a welcoming community hub for meetings and small conferences. Coordinates with UR units (Marketing Communications, Graphic Services, Web Services and Government Relations) to ensure consistent messaging branding and promotional support for all events. Prepares summary reports and recommendations for UR leadership to inform future event planning and demonstrate return on investment. Other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Possession of a baccalaureate degree in Communications, Marketing, Public Relations, Event Management, Hospitality Management, Social Sciences, Business Administration or related field and three (3) year(s) of progressively responsible professional experience with responsibilities for event planning, coordination and management; or any equivalent combination of education and/or professional work experience which provides the required education, knowledge, skills and abilities as indicated. Considerable working knowledge of principles, practices and techniques in the area of event planning, coordination and management as demonstrated by the broad knowledge of the full range of pertinent standard and evolving concepts, principles and methodologies. Considerable working knowledge and understanding of applicable federal and state laws, rules, regulations and theories and systems associated with event planning, coordination and management. Demonstrated ability to resolve wide ranging complex problems through the use of creative reasoning and logic to accurately determine the cause of the problems and the resolution of the problems in an effective, innovative and timely manner. Demonstrated ability to interpret and present information and ideas clearly and accurately in writing, verbally and by preparation of reports and other materials. Demonstrated ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with internal and external organizations, groups, team leaders and members, and individuals. Demonstrated ability to operate a personal computer, apply word processing software, and event management platforms, and project management tools. For supervisory work, demonstrated ability to lead subordinates, manage work priorities and projects, and manage employee relations. Supplemental Minimum Qualifications: Working knowledge of procurement, purchasing, and fiscal processes sufficient to plan event budgets, coordinate vendor contracts, and ensure compliance with institutional policies and procedures. Demonstrated ability to conceptualize and execute creative event concepts that engage diverse audiences and advance institutional goals. Demonstrated ability to coordinate and lead cross-functional teams to accomplish complex, multi-stakeholder projects under deadline pressure. Demonstrated ability to plan, organize, and manage large-scale events involving multiple departments, divisions, and external partners. Demonstrated ability to navigate complex procurement, fiscal, and administrative processes with attention to detail, accuracy, and compliance. Demonstrated creative thinking and ability to translate event concepts into well-executed, engaging experiences. Demonstrated ability to multitask and handle a wide variety of assignments simultaneously on deadline. Desirable Qualifications: Experience working with and knowledge of post-secondary education and its organizational structure, policies, and procedures. Experience with community engagement, facility coordination, or conference services in a higher education or public-sector setting. Proficient communication, orally and written, of the Hawaiian language, including an understanding of basic greetings, responses, and commonly used expressions. Demonstrated cultural competency and ability to plan and execute events that reflect Indigenous knowledge, values, and protocols. Experience incorporating Native Hawaiian and Indigenous perspectives into event design, community engagement, and institutional programming. To Apply: Click on the “Apply” button on the top right corner of the screen to complete an application and attach each required document. A complete application must include: Cover letter explaining how each minimum and desirable qualification is met. Current resume. The names and addresses, email addresses and telephone numbers of three [3] current professional references. Transcript(s) showing degrees and course work appropriate to the position (copies are acceptable; however, original official transcripts will be required prior to employment). Please do not include any self-identifying photos. Please redact references to Social Security number and birth date on transcript copies. Copy of diplomas will NOT be accepted. Documents issued from an institution outside the United States of America require a course-by-course analysis with an equivalency statement from an agency having membership with the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services, Inc., verifying the degree equivalency to that of an accredited institution within the USA. Expense of the evaluation shall be borne by the applicant. All requested documents/information become the property of the University. All minimum qualifications must be met by the closing date. Incomplete applications will not be considered. Failure to submit all required documents and reference information shall deem an application to be incomplete. Note: If you have not applied for a position before using NeoGov, you will need to create an account. Inquiries: Amy Kalili, akalili@hawaii.edu EEO, Clery Act, ADA The University of Hawai'i is an Equal Opportunity Institution and is committed to a policy of nondiscrimination in employment, including on the basis of veteran and disability status.  For more information, visit: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/policies/ Employment is contingent on satisfying employment eligibility verification requirements of the Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986; reference checks of previous employers; and for certain positions, criminal history record checks. In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, annual campus crime statistics for the University of Hawai'i may be viewed at: https://www.hawaii.edu/titleix/help/campus-security/ , or a paper copy may be obtained upon request from the respective UH Campus Security or Administrative Services Office. In accordance with Article 10 of the unit 08 collective bargaining agreement, bargaining unit members receive priority consideration for APT job vacancies. As a result, external or non BU 08 applicants may not be considered for some APT vacancies. BU 08 members with re-employment rights or priority status are responsible for informing the hiring unit of their status. Accommodation Request: The University of Hawai'i complies with the provisions of the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). Applicants requiring a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process should contact the EEO coordinator directly. Determination on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis. For further information, please refer to the following link: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/accommodation-request/ Equal Opportunity Employer / Veterans / Disabled Employer University of Hawaii Department University of Hawai'i at Hilo Address 200 W. Kawili Street Hilo, Hawaii, 96720 Website http://workatuh.hawaii.edu Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Career Opportunities at the University of Hawai'i Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this setting does not apply, however, you can review your right on our privacy policy . If you require further assistance, please email privacy@neogov.com × Accessibility Statement At Governmentjobs.com, Inc. d/b/a NEOGOV, we recognize the importance of making our products\n                    and services accessible to all individuals, including those with disabilities, and are continually\n                    working to improve the experience for all users. Commitment to Accessibility We are committed to following best practices, including the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines\n                    (WCAG) 2.1, Level AA, to the extent feasible, however, we do not warrant compliance with these\n                    standards or any other accessibility standards. We are continually enhancing our platforms to\n                    ensure greater accessibility, and we actively seek out opportunities to improve accessibility features. Ongoing Enhancements Accessibility is an ongoing effort, and we are regularly updating our technology, services, and content\n                    to address accessibility barriers. Our team is dedicated to identifying areas for improvement and\n                    making enhancements that allow all users, regardless of their abilities, to fully engage with our\n                    services. Feedback and Assistance We value feedback from our users. If you encounter any accessibility barriers while using our services\n                    or have suggestions on how we can improve, please reach out to us at accessibility@neogov.com.\n                    We will make every effort to resolve any concerns and consider alternative options where possible. Thank you for choosing NEOGOV. We remain dedicated to improving accessibility and creating an\n                    inclusive experience for all. University of Hawai'i Career Opportunities at the University of Hawai'i Menu Close Menu University of Hawai'i Career Opportunities at the University of Hawai'i Civil Service Positions (Internal Applicants Only) Job Interest Card About UH Benefits University of Hawai'i's System Office of Human Resources Annual Campus Crime Stats Employment Related Posters/Brochures Help & Support Translate Support Job Application Job Details Applying as: | Support Close Close Cancel Clear SIGN Save We've updated our Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. Please, read and accept changes. Effective date: August 19, 2025 NEOGOV PRIVACY POLICY Contents 1. Introduction; Scope of this Policy. 2. Where We Are a Service Provider. 3. Personal Data We Collect About You and Why. 4. Cookies and Similar Tracking Technologies. 5. Online Analytics and Advertising. 6. Information We Disclose. 7. International Users. 8. Your Data Rights and Choices. 9. Notice to California Residents. 10. Your Rights and Control under EU GDPR. 11. Data Security and Integrity. 12. Retention and Removal. 13. Right to Revise. 14. Contact Details. 15. Privacy Contacts. Introduction; Scope of this Policy. The purpose of this Privacy Policy (the “Policy”) is to describe how we collect, use, store, protect, and disclose personal data online and offline either via our websites or related applications. This Policy applies to personal data we collect or use, and applications owned or controlled by Governmentjobs.com, Inc. (DBA “NEOGOV”), including our related brands NEOGOV.com, NEOED.com, PowerDMS.com, Governmentjobs.com, Schooljobs.com, and our mobile app(s) (collectively referred to as the “Services”), or affiliated companies (collectively referred to herein as “Governmentjobs”, \"Schooljobs\", “NEOGOV”, “NEOED”, “PowerDMS”, “we”, “us”, or “our”). By using any part of the Services you agree that you have read this Policy, your personal data will be processed as described herein, and you agree to be bound by this Policy. This Policy is incorporated into our Terms of Use . Definitions not explicitly defined herein shall retain the meaning as prescribed in the Terms of Use . Any dispute related to privacy is subject to the Terms of Use and this Policy, including limitations on liability. This Policy does not apply to (1) personal data controlled by our Customers (employers that utilize our Services, described further below), which is governed by our separate agreements and related data processing agreements with such"
