    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/hawaiiedu/jobs/5467266/admin-fiscal-support-specialist-0081980t": {
      "title": "Admin & Fiscal Support Specialist (0081980T)",
      "description": "Career Opportunities at the University of Hawai'i | University of Hawai'i For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Admin & Fiscal Support Specialist (0081980T) | University of Hawai'i page has loaded. Admin & Fiscal Support Specialist (0081980T) | University of Hawai'i page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Career Opportunities at the University of Hawai'i Menu Career Opportunities at the University of Hawai'i Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. University of Hawai'i powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Admin & Fiscal Support Specialist (0081980T) Print Apply ﻿ Admin & Fiscal Support Specialist (0081980T) Salary See Position Description Location UH System Offices, Honolulu, HI Job Type Full-Time Temporary Job Number 2026-01896 Department Office of the Vice President for Research and Innovation System Division Office of Strategic Initiatives Opening Date 08/31/2026 Closing Date 9/14/2026 11:59 PM Hawaii Position Number: 0081980T Description Title: Administrative and Fiscal Support Specialist Position: 0081980T Hiring Unit: Office of the Vice President for Research and Innovation (OVPRI), Office of Strategic Health Initiatives (OSHI) Location: Manoa Campus Date Posted: August 31, 2026 Closing Date: September 14, 2026 @ 11:59pm Band: A Salary: salary schedules and placement information Additional Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience. Full Time/Part Time: Full-Time Month: 11-month Temporary/Permanent: Temporary Other Conditions: Position is annually renewable contingent on satisfactory performance and availability of funds. This is not a remote position. Duties and Responsibilities (NOTE: ** denotes Essential Functions) **Serves as the Administrative and Fiscal Support Specialist for the University of Hawai?i System Office of Strategic Health Initiatives (OSHI) in support of the Education, Training, and Policy Core of the U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs (VA) Center for Pacific Islander Veteran Health (CPIVH), and provides program coordination, administrative, fiscal, and communications support across OSHI programs. **Provides staff support in the following field of assignment or subject matter area: program coordination, administrative and fiscal operations, and communications support for federally funded health programs and initiatives. **Provides assistance to and takes direction from higher level professionals who manage and control programs and functions. **Plans, coordinates, analyzes, and/or supports work within the subject matter area of day-to-day project operations, including calendar and meeting coordination, scheduling, note-taking, travel arrangements, and coordination of staffing and supply needs for the community engagement and curriculum teams. **Serves as a point of contact for project staff, contracted specialists, community partners, University offices, and federal sponsor counterparts. **Assists leadership in the performance of administrative tasks including processing requisitions, purchase orders, tr [1] [2] avel requests, P-Card transactions, inventory control, and other expenditures. **Implements and configures management procedures, e.g., deliverable tracking systems, quality control checklists, file organization protocols, and version control practices, for the identification, control, and accounting of data, e.g., project records, deliverable documentation, meeting records, and contract files. **Assists by compiling checklists, tracking due dates and assigned owners, and documenting corrective actions in the development, management, planning, review, and application of quality assurance and quality control techniques, principles, disciplines, procedures, and requirements in support of the development and production of contract deliverables. **Supports staff in the performance of specific work assignments, such as preparing weekly, monthly, quarterly, and annual reports to the federal sponsor, tracking delivery of key milestones within set timelines, and assembling supporting documentation. **Plans, schedules, collects data, and assists in the analysis of project budgets, expenditures, and grant and contract reporting. **Develops, coordinates, and conducts logistical planning for project meetings and events, including monthly community engagement meetings and an annual provider summit, in coordination with project staff and community partners. **Writes, edits, and coordinates approval of program documentation, e.g., meeting summaries, informational fact sheets, newsletters, website content, and event promotion materials. **Assists staff in grant and contract application preparation and submission. **Uses standard software, e.g., Google Workspace, Microsoft Office, Zoom, and Canva, to create and edit content and maintain project records. Performs other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Education and Professional Work Experience: Possession of a baccalaureate degree in fields related to public health, health sciences, public policy, economics, or political science and one (1) year of progressively responsible professional experience with responsibilities for program coordination, administrative support, fiscal or grant support, and/or communications; or any equivalent combination of education and/or professional work experience which provides the required education, knowledge, skills and abilities as indicated. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Functional knowledge of principles, practices and techniques in the area of program coordination, administrative support, fiscal or grant support, and/or communications demonstrated by knowledge, understanding and ability to apply concepts, terminology. Functional knowledge and understanding of principles, theories, federal and state laws, rules, regulations and systems associated with the administration of federally funded contracts and grants. Demonstrated ability to recognize problems, identify possible causes and resolve the full range problems that may commonly occur in the area of program coordination, administrative support, fiscal or grant support, and/or communications. Demonstrated ability to understand oral and written documentation, write reports and procedures, and communicate effectively in a variety of situations. Demonstrated ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with internal and external organizations, groups, team members and individuals. Demonstrated ability to operate a personal computer, apply word processing software, and apply spreadsheet, presentation, videoconferencing, and graphic design software, e.g., Microsoft Office, Google Workspace, Zoom, Canva, and/or Adobe Creative Suite. Supplemental Minimum Qualifications Excellent organization, writing, presentation, and communications skills. Demonstrated ability to work in a fast-paced environment with frequent interaction with team members and OVPRI management, fiscal manager, vendors, researchers, staff from other institutions and other UH units. Demonstrated ability to manage multiple assignments concurrently and maintain a pleasant, courteous attitude when dealing with others. Demonstrated ability to solve problems using critical thinking that reflects sound judgement and analysis. Ability to attend occasional meetings scheduled outside of standard business hours to align with Pacific and U.S. mainland time zones. Ability to travel, as required. Desirable Qualifications Experience supporting federally funded projects, contracts, or grants within higher education, government, or a nonprofit setting. Familiarity with the University of Hawai?i System and its fiscal, procurement, travel, and human resources policies and procedures. Knowledge of, or lived experience with, Native Hawaiian, Pacific Islander, and/or U.S.-Affiliated Pacific Islander communities, languages, and cultural protocols. Experience working with or on behalf of Veterans, military-connected populations, or health care organizations serving them. Experience coordinating meetings, trainings, conferences, or community events, including virtual and hybrid formats spanning multiple time zones. Experience with graphic design and content creation tools such as Canva or the Adobe Creative Suite. To Apply: Select the \"Apply\" button in the top right corner of the screen; first-time NeoGov users will need to create an account. Please ensure your application includes the following materials: Cover Letter: A letter detailing your interest and how you meet both the minimum and desirable qualifications. All minimum qualifications must be met by the closing date to be considered. Resume/CV: A current professional resume or curriculum vitae. Professional References: The names, telephone numbers, and email addresses of three (3) professional references. Unofficial Transcripts: Copies of unofficial transcripts are required for the application, though official versions must be provided upon hire. Please note that copies of diplomas and academic summaries are not acceptable substitutes. Foreign Credential Evaluation: For degrees earned outside the U.S., you must provide a course-by-course analysis and equivalency statement from a NACES-member agency at your own expense. Important Note: To protect your privacy, do not include any photos, Social Security Numbers, or dates of birth in your packet. Only the most recent application will be reviewed, and all submitted materials become the property of the University of Hawai’i. Please ensure all documents are complete and legible to be considered by the search committee. Incomplete applications will not be considered. Inquiries: Lara Studzinski; larastud@hawaii.edu EEO, Clery Act, ADA The University of Hawai'i is an Equal Opportunity Institution and is committed to a policy of nondiscrimination in employment, including on the basis of veteran and disability status.  For more information, visit: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/policies/ Employment is contingent on satisfying employment eligibility verification requirements of the Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986; reference checks of previous employers; and for certain positions, criminal history record checks. In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, annual campus crime statistics for the University of Hawai'i may be viewed at: https://www.hawaii.edu/titleix/help/campus-security/ , or a paper copy may be obtained upon request from the respective UH Campus Security or Administrative Services Office. In accordance with Article 10 of the unit 08 collective bargaining agreement, bargaining unit members receive priority consideration for APT job vacancies. As a result, external or non BU 08 applicants may not be considered for some APT vacancies. BU 08 members with re-employment rights or priority status are responsible for informing the hiring unit of their status. Accommodation Request: The University of Hawai'i complies with the provisions of the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). Applicants requiring a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process should contact the EEO coordinator directly. Determination on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis. For further information, please refer to the following link: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/accommodation-request/ Employer University of Hawaii Website http://workatuh.hawaii.edu Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Career Opportunities at the University of Hawai'i Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this setting does not apply, however, you can review your right on our privacy policy . If you require further assistance, please email privacy@neogov.com × Accessibility Statement At Governmentjobs.com, Inc. d/b/a NEOGOV, we recognize the importance of making our products\n                    and services accessible to all individuals, including those with disabilities, and are continually\n                    working to improve the experience for all users. Commitment to Accessibility We are committed to following best practices, including the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines\n                    (WCAG) 2.1, Level AA, to the extent feasible, however, we do not warrant compliance with these\n                    standards or any other accessibility standards. We are continually enhancing our platforms to\n                    ensure greater accessibility, and we actively seek out opportunities to improve accessibility features. Ongoing Enhancements Accessibility is an ongoing effort, and we are regularly updating our technology, services, and content\n                    to address accessibility barriers. Our team is dedicated to identifying areas for improvement and\n                    making enhancements that allow all users, regardless of their abilities, to fully engage with our\n                    services. Feedback and Assistance We value feedback from our users. If you encounter any accessibility barriers while using our services\n                    or have suggestions on how we can improve, please reach out to us at accessibility@neogov.com.\n                    We will make every effort to resolve any concerns and consider alternative options where possible. Thank you for choosing NEOGOV. We remain dedicated to improving accessibility and creating an\n                    inclusive experience for all. University of Hawai'i Career Opportunities at the University of Hawai'i Menu Close Menu University of Hawai'i Career Opportunities at the University of Hawai'i Civil Service Positions (Internal Applicants Only) Job Interest Card About UH Benefits University of Hawai'i's System Office of Human Resources Annual Campus Crime Stats Employment Related Posters/Brochures Help & Support Translate Support Job Application Job Details Applying as: | Support Close Close Cancel Clear SIGN Save We've updated our Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. Please, read and accept changes. Effective date: August 19, 2025 NEOGOV PRIVACY POLICY Contents 1. Introduction; Scope of this Policy. 2. Where We Are a Service Provider. 3. Personal Data We Collect About You and Why. 4. Cookies and Similar Tracking Technologies. 5. Online Analytics and Advertising. 6. Information We Disclose. 7. International Users. 8. Your Data Rights and Choices. 9. Notice to California Residents. 10. Your Rights and Control under EU GDPR. 11. Data Security and Integrity. 12. Retention and Removal. 13.