    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/hawaiiedu/jobs/5433066/associate-professor-cc-health-science-coordinator-0085262": {
      "title": "Associate Professor, CC (Health Science Coordinator, 0085262)",
      "description": "Career Opportunities at the University of Hawai'i | University of Hawai'i For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Associate Professor, CC (Health Science Coordinator, 0085262) | University of Hawai'i page has loaded. Associate Professor, CC (Health Science Coordinator, 0085262) | University of Hawai'i page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Career Opportunities at the University of Hawai'i Menu Career Opportunities at the University of Hawai'i Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. University of Hawai'i powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Associate Professor, CC (Health Science Coordinator, 0085262) Print Apply ﻿ Associate Professor, CC (Health Science Coordinator, 0085262) Location Hawai'i CC, Hilo, HI Job Type Full-Time Permanent Job Number 2026-01691 Department Hawai'i Community College - Career and Technical Education Division Nursing and Allied Health Opening Date 08/24/2026 Closing Date 9/16/2026 11:59 PM Hawaii Position Number: 0085626 Description Title:                                                           Associate Professor, CC (Health Sciences Coordinator) Position Number:                                      0085262 Hiring Unit:                                                Hawaii Community College Location:                                                    Hilo Date Posted:                                             August 24, 2026 Closing Date:                                            September 16, 2026 Salary Information:                                   Pay to commensurate with education and experience Monthly Type:                                           11 Month Tenure Track:                                            Tenure Full Time/Part Time:                                  Full Time Temporary/Permanent:                            Permanent Other Conditions: General funds, to begin approximately November 2026, pending availability of funds and actual staffing requirements. This assignment may include teaching on- and off-campus, day or evening classes, weekend classes, and distance education assignments using multiple teaching methodologies; and travel between Hilo, West Hawaii, and other off-site locations.  Position may be converted from 11 to 9 months or 9 to 11 months based on operational needs. Duties and Responsibilities: Accountable and responsible for all aspects of the Hawaii CC campus' Health Sciences Division, comprising of Nursing and Allied Health programs, and the Fire Science Programs including active engagement appropriate to the challenges of educating diverse communities of people on Hawaii Island. Works with Hawaii CC and UH System Administration to sustain, improve and develop the Division’s academic programs, which includes non-credit programs. Plans and suggests updates to the division/department curriculum, courses, and programs. Prepares, maintains and monitors division/department’s budgets. Assists in securing extramural funding to support the division’s programs. Liaise with college offices for the procurement, maintenance, and inventory of the division equipment. Serves as liaison, keeping division/department members informed of general campus activities and representing the division/department views to the administration. Assists in and/or identifies and resolves division/departmental concerns. Assists in and/or establishes and maintains positive work relationships among faculty, staff and administrators within campus structure. Communicates with clinical agencies, national accreditation agencies, the Hawaii State Board of Nursing, the Hawaii State Center for Nursing, and the Hawaii CC Advisory Committees. Leads accreditation and approval activities following the State and national accreditors’ regulations, standards, requirements, and current practices, including self-studies and campus visits. Prepares and submits annual accreditation reports to the state and national accreditors. Prepares annual program reviews and yearly nursing program systematic reviews; and contributes data for the Hawaii CC accreditation reports and other reports for other programs within the division. Coordinates the assessment of program and course outcomes data. Assists in Student and Faculty Handbook updates. Maintains and secures MOUs with clinical sites/health care organizations as needed. Plans and facilitates regular faculty meetings to facilitate communication and faculty participation in planning, implementing, and evaluating the curriculum. Supervises and evaluates Faculty, Staff, Lecturer, and Student Assistant personnel. Participates in the recruitment of division personnel. Leads and assists faculty with problem-solving to support optimal student outcomes including remediation and/or dismissal. Facilitates faculty educational development and services within the division, Hawaii CC campus, University System, and the community. Facilitates posting and scheduling of courses ensuring that the student information system reflects all faculty workload. Assists in implementing an orientation process for new faculty and recommending faculty mentors to guide new faculty. Facilitates student recruitment, orientations, and advising and guides the academic progression committee. Facilitates faculty and student clinical clearance by applicable deadlines. Facilitates resolution of student academic grievances. Facilitates student evaluations of instruction. Plans and facilitates annual program graduation ceremonies and Student Pinning Ceremony Committee. Coordinates and updates the division or department section of the campus catalog of courses. Updates information on the division’s websites, including an update on the nursing laboratory resources website. Demonstrates professionalism and provides quality service in accordance with Hawaii Community College's values. Participates in college and community service. Teach course(s) in Health Sciences programs as needed but a minimum of one course per academic year. Other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Master’s Degree in Nursing, with academic credits in curriculum development, evaluation, or teaching methods. Academic preparation for administration or administrative experience or both. Attainment of academic rank of C-4 or a demonstrated record of comparable professional experience. Equivalency is nine years of experience related to Nursing education, teaching, curriculum development, this is in addition to meeting the educations qualifications. At least one year of hospital experience in one of the areas of teaching responsibility. Preferably this experience will have been gained within the last five years of date of application. RN eligible for Hawaii State License. License required by effective date of employment. Desirable Qualification: Demonstrated ability to work effectively with a multicultural healthcare community. Demonstrated record of scholarship, teaching, and service, qualifying for appointment at senior faculty rank. Ability to prepare and maintain comprehensive records and reports. Ability to communicate effectively both orally and in writing with the health care community, public, students, faculty, and staff. Ability to work flexible hours. Demonstrated commitment and/or experience supporting the success of students. Application Submission : Click on the \"Apply\" button to complete an application and attach the following required documents ( REDACT social security number and date of birth on all uploaded documents ). Cover letter outlining how you meet minimum and desirable qualifications; Names and contact information of three (3) professional references; Resume. A Copy of your academic transcript(s) appropriate to the position MUST be attached in order to verify all courses completed and/or degree conferred (unofficial transcripts are acceptable; copies of diplomas will NOT be accepted). If transcript(s) are not provided, the candidate’s degree(s) or coursework will not be considered. Official transcripts are required at the time of hire. Transcripts issued outside the United States of America require a course-by-course analysis with an equivalency statement from an agency having membership with the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services, Inc., verifying the degree equivalency to that of an accredited institution within the USA will be required before date of hire. Expense of the evaluation shall be borne by the applicant; NOTE: Minimum qualifications (degree and credits) must be met by the effective date of appointment. Letters of recommendation are welcome. The application will be considered incomplete if material is unreadable, or required documents are not submitted by the closing date. Incomplete applications will not be considered. All documents/information submitted become the property of Hawaii Community College and will not be returned. If multiple applications are submitted, only the last application received will be considered. If you have not applied for a position before using NEOGOV, you will need to create an account. Inquiries:  808-934-2525 EEO, Clery Act, ADA The University of Hawai'i is an Equal Opportunity Institution and is committed to a policy of nondiscrimination in employment, including on the basis of veteran and disability status.  For more information, visit: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/policies/ Employment is contingent on satisfying employment eligibility verification requirements of the Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986; reference checks of previous employers; and for certain positions, criminal history record checks. In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, annual campus crime statistics for the University of Hawai'i may be viewed at: https://www.hawaii.edu/titleix/help/campus-security/ , or a paper copy may be obtained upon request from the respective UH Campus Security or Administrative Services Office. Accommodation Request: The University of Hawai'i complies with the provisions of the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). Applicants requiring a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process should contact the EEO coordinator directly. Determination on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis. For further information, please refer to the following link: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/accommodation-request/ Employer University of Hawaii Department Hawai'i Community College - Career and Technical Education Address 1175 Manono Street Hilo, Hawaii, 96720 Website http://workatuh.hawaii.edu Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Career Opportunities at the University of Hawai'i Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: L