    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/hawaiiedu/jobs/5128131/educational-specialist-simulation-lab-tech-0079534t": {
      "title": "Educational Specialist (Simulation Lab Tech) 0079534T",
      "description": "Career Opportunities at the University of Hawai'i | University of Hawai'i For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Educational Specialist (Simulation Lab Tech) 0079534T | University of Hawai'i page has loaded. Educational Specialist (Simulation Lab Tech) 0079534T | University of Hawai'i page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Career Opportunities at the University of Hawai'i Menu Career Opportunities at the University of Hawai'i Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. University of Hawai'i powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Educational Specialist (Simulation Lab Tech) 0079534T Print Apply ﻿ Educational Specialist (Simulation Lab Tech) 0079534T Location UH Manoa, Honolulu, HI Job Type Full-Time Temporary Job Number 2025-02264 Department University of Hawai'i at Manoa - School of Nursing and Dental Hygiene - Dean's Office Opening Date 08/19/2026 Closing Date 9/11/2026 11:59 PM Hawaii Position Number: 0079534T Description Title: Educational Specialist (Simulation Lab Technician) Position Number: 0079534T Hiring Unit: School of Nursing and Dental Hygiene (Translational Health Science Simulation Center) Location: Manoa Campus / Honolulu Date Posted: August 19, 2026 (Readvertisement) Closing Date: July September 11, 2026 Band: A Minimum Monthly Salary: Salary Schedules and Placement Information Full Time/Part Time: Full-Time, 100% Temporary/Permanent: Temporary Other Conditions: This position will support the operations of the University of Hawaii at Manoa School of Nursing and Dental Hygiene (SONDH) UH Translational Health Science Simulation Center (THSSC). The UH THSSC brings real-life scenarios to the classroom so that students can gain the experience, confidence and skills they need to provide quality care. The center integrates state-of-the-art equipment, electronic patient records and practices currently used by the state’s leading medical centers. Click HERE for a virtual/video tour of the THSSC, and see our simulation techs and students in action for an elevated experience in this state-of-the-art healthcare technology. The position is expected to begin this Fall 2026 semester. Renewal of appointment is dependent on performance, program needs and/or availability of funds. To know more about the UH at Manoa, SONDH, go to: https://nursing.hawaii.edu/ . Duties and Responsibilities: ** Serve as Simulation Lab Technician responsible for the set-up, operation, and maintenance of the simulation equipment in the UH Translational Health Science Simulation Center (THSSC). ** Operate and control manikin functions; provide verbal responses in scenarios; assist with simulated patient sessions; troubleshoot technical issues in real-time; and other duties to ensure smooth operation of the simulation experience. ** Clean and maintain equipment, supplies and facility after simulation sessions. ** Assist simulation specialists with the demonstration of THSSC equipment including simulators and the standardized patient program. ** Assist THSSC team members with integrating new equipment and software into the functions of the Center. ** Provide technical support to simulation specialists in the training and orientation of internal and external users. ** Assist with programming scenarios into simulator equipment, collaborate with team to revise existing scripts to correspond to the goals of a particular session and/or audience's level of experience, and develops directions for each simulator instructor. ** Prepare facility, medical supplies, materials and instruments, and equipment for simulation sessions for High Fidelity, Low Fidelity (dry lab), standardized patients, faculty and others. ** Manage and maintain inventories of simulators, equipment, and supplies, and keep software and hardware configurations updated. ** Assist with the annual and mid-year equipment preventive maintenance and inventory for THSSC. ** Conduct educational tours of THSSC. Participate in departmental strategic planning and orientation/training of new THSSC staff. Maintains files of simulation cases and modules. Other duties as assigned. (**) Denotes Essential Functions Minimum Qualifications: Possession of a baccalaureate degree in education, social science, communications, education technology, healthcare or related field and one (1) year of progressively responsible professional experience with responsibilities for customer service in a laboratory setting, training, or operations support in an education setting, health care; or any equivalent combination of education and/or professional work experience which provides the required education, knowledge, skills and abilities as indicated. Functional knowledge of principles, practices and techniques in training, service-oriented occupations or operational support demonstrated by knowledge, understanding and ability to apply concepts, terminology. Functional knowledge and understanding of principles, theories, federal and state laws, rules, regulations and systems associated with training, interpersonal relationships, or operational support. Demonstrated ability to recognize problems, identify possible causes and resolve the full range problems that may commonly occur in the training, servicing situations, or operational support environment. Demonstrated ability to understand oral and written documentation, write reports and procedures, and communicate effectively in a variety of situations. Demonstrated ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with internal and external organizations, groups, team members and individuals. Demonstrated ability to operate a personal computer and apply word processing software. Demonstrated ability to acquire new skills and learn new techniques to operate technology and equipment in a health care training and research environment. Demonstrated ability to problem-solve and make quick, decisive decisions in a changing health training and research environment. Desirable Qualifications: Experience with simulation learning specifically with high-fidelity, manikin and standardized/simulated patient learning. Experience working with students and faculty in an academic or research environment Familiarity with technology resources utilized in learning or research centers such as computer-based equipment, data bases, and audio visual systems. Experience providing logistical facility support, such as class, laboratory, meeting, or other activity set-up. Familiarity with medical instruments and equipment used in medical facility. To Apply: Note: If you have not applied for a position before using NeoGov, you will need to create an account. Click on the \"Apply\" button on the top right corner of the screen to complete an application and attach required documents. Applicant must submit the following: Cover letter indicating how you satisfy the minimum and desirable qualifications; Resume; Names and contact information (telephone number and email addresses) of three (3) professional references; and Copies of unofficial transcripts (official transcripts will be required at the time of hire).  Academic record/grade summaries and copy of diplomas are NOT ACCEPTABLE. Documents issued from an institution outside the United States of America require a course-by-course analysis with an equivalency statement from an agency having membership with the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services, Inc., verifying the degree equivalency to that of an accredited institution within the USA. Expense of the evaluation shall be borne by the applicant. NOTE: If multiple applications are received from the same candidate, only the last one will be reviewed. Please do not include any self-identifying photos they will be redacted. PLEASE REDACT Social Security #s and birth dates on transcript copies. All submitted items become the property of the University of Hawaii and will not be returned. Only complete applications will be passed on to the search committee for consideration. No late applications will be accepted. Inquiries: Corie O. Fulgencio-Arre, HR Specialist; mcfa@hawaii.edu EEO, Clery Act, ADA The University of Hawai'i is an Equal Opportunity Institution and is committed to a policy of nondiscrimination in employment, including on the basis of veteran and disability status. For more information, visit: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/policies/ Employment is contingent on satisfying employment eligibility verification requirements of the Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986; reference checks of previous employers; and for certain positions, criminal history record checks. In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, annual campus crime statistics for the University of Hawai'i may be viewed at: https://www.hawaii.edu/titleix/help/campus-security/ , or adpaper copy may be obtained upon request from the respective UH Campus Security or Administrative Services Office. In accordance with Article 10 of the unit 08 collective bargaining agreement, bargaining unit members receive priority consideration for APT job vacancies. As a result, external or non BU 08 applicants may not be considered for some APT vacancies. BU 08 members with re-employment rights or priority status are responsible for informing the hiring unit of their status. Accommodation Request: The University of Hawai'i complies with the provisions of the Americans with Disabilities Act(ADA). Applicants requiring a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process should contact the EEO coordinator directly. Determination on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis. For further information, please refer to the following link: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/accommodation-request/ Employer University of Hawaii Website http://workatuh.hawaii.edu Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Career Opportunities at the University of Hawai'i Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this setting does not apply, however, you can review your right on our privacy policy . If you require further assistance, please email privacy@neogov.com × Accessibility Statement At Governmentjobs.com, Inc. d/b/a NEOGOV, we recognize the importance of making our products\n                    and services accessible to all individuals, including those with disabilities, and are continually\n                    working to improve the experience for all users. Commitment to Accessibility We are committed to following best practices, including the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines\n                    (WCAG) 2.1, Level AA, to the extent feasible, however, we do not warrant compliance with these\n                    standards or any other accessibility standards. We are continually enhancing our platforms to\n                    ensure greater accessibility, and we actively seek out opportunities to improve accessibility features. Ongoing Enhancements Accessibility is an ongoing effort, and we are regularly updating our technology, services, and content\n                    to address accessibility barriers. Our team is dedicated to identifying areas for improvement and\n                    making enhancements that allow all users, regardless of their abilities, to fully engage with our\n                    services. Feedback and Assistance We value feedback from our users. If you encounter any accessibility barriers while using our services\n                    or have suggestions on how we can improve, please reach out to us at accessibility@neogov.com.\n                    We will make every effort to resolve any concerns and consider alternative options where possible. Thank you for choosing NEOGOV. We remain dedicated to improving accessibility and creating an\n                    inclusive experience for all. University of Hawai'i Career Opportunities at the University of Hawai'i Menu Close Menu University of Hawai'i Career Opportunities at the University of Hawai'i Civil Service Positions (Internal Applicants Only) Job Interest Card About UH Benefits University of Hawai'i's System Office of Human Resources Annual Campus Crime Stats Employment Related Posters/Brochures Help & Support Translate Support Job Application Job Details Applying as: | Support Close Close Cancel Clear SIGN Save We've updated our Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. Please, read and accept changes. Effective date: August 19, 2025 NEOGOV PRIVACY POLICY Contents 1. 