    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/hawaiiedu/jobs/5428134/professor-0083413": {
      "title": "Professor",
      "description": "Career Opportunities at the University of Hawai'i | University of Hawai'i For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Professor (0083413) | University of Hawai'i page has loaded. Professor (0083413) | University of Hawai'i page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Career Opportunities at the University of Hawai'i Menu Career Opportunities at the University of Hawai'i Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. University of Hawai'i powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Professor (0083413) Print Apply ﻿ Professor (0083413) Salary $0.00 Semi-Monthly Location UH Manoa - JABSOM, Queen's Medical Center - Honolulu, HI Job Type Full-Time Permanent Job Number 2026-01651 Department University of Hawai'i at Manoa - John A. Burns School of Medicine Division Medicine Opening Date 07/28/2026 Closing Date Continuous Position Number: 83413 Description Title: Professor (H5M11) Position Number: 0083413 Hiring Unit: UHM John A. Burns School of Medicine, Department of Medicine Location: Queen’s Medical Center Date Posted: July 28, 2026 Closing Date: Rolling recruitment Salary Information: Salary commensurate with qualifications and experience. Monthly Type: 11 Month Tenure Track: Tenure Full Time/Part Time: 100% Temporary/Permanent: Permanent Funding: G-funds Other Conditions: Full-time, tenure track, annually renewable depending on performance, departmental needs and/or funding availability. To begin approximately March 2027, subject to position clearance and availability of funds. First review begins August 19, 2026, with continuous recruitment until filled. This position may also be funded by extramural funds. Duties and Responsibilities: Participates in the development of principles and processes to guide the strengthening of academic programs in the department of medicine with respect to Undergraduate Medical Education (UME) and Graduate Medical Education (GME) program evaluation, and similar academic endeavors within John A. Burns School of Medicine (JABSOM) clinical affiliates. Assumes potential leadership roles as requested, which may include serving as Department Chair for Medicine and in a leadership role in an affiliated faculty practice medical group. Participate in strategic planning and implementation at the school level (e.g, relevant to the development of the department of medicine and JABSOM) and collaborate with the Queen’s University Medical Group (QUMG), Queen’s Health Systems (QHS), Hawai‘i Pacific Health (HPH), Hawai‘i Pacific Health Medical Group (HPHMG), and other JABSOM clinical affiliates, providing a unique academic clinical faculty and clinician scientist perspective to align clinical operations with the academic mission. Participates in developing clinical research and service programs that include JABSOM learners and faculty and are designed to strengthen the innovative delivery of health care within JABSOM clinical affiliates, with a focus on the disciplines of medicine. Assists with the maintenance of the Liaison Committee on Medical Education (LCME) and Accreditation Council for Graduate Medical Education (ACGME) for medicine and subspecialty experiences and programs based at all JABSOM clinical affiliates with such experiences. Oversees clinical quality improvement initiatives, curriculum development, and faculty evaluations. Serve as principal investigator for clinical services grant/contract proposals. Serve as mentor for students, residents, fellows, and faculty, and promote a strong clinical faculty development program based on H-series promotion goals. Promotes ongoing professional growth and development by participating in continuing medical education, leadership training, professional conferences, and other learning opportunities relevant to the practice of medicine and academic healthcare leadership. Conduct and publish research in areas affecting human health, patient care, or methods and techniques of medical education. Build a vigorous departmental research program with extramural funding. Engage in continuous learning through literature reviews, active participation in in-service meetings and workshops, and system-wide educational initiatives to stay current with academic best practices. Perform other related duties as assigned to support the mission and vision of the University of Hawai’i and JABSOM, in close coordination with the missions of JABSOM’s clinical affiliates. Perform related work as assigned by the Dean. Minimum Qualifications: MD degree or equivalent medical degree from an accredited medical school. Minimum of four years in the rank of Associate Professor, or ten years of other health care experience, or a total of ten years of teaching in the rank of Associate Professor and other health care experience, or one year in the rank of Professor at another health care school of recognized standing. Current Board certification in Internal Medicine with ongoing Maintenance of Certification, and any relevant subspecialty boards. Eligible for or currently holds an unrestricted Hawai’i Medical License. Evidence of excellence in teaching, national or international recognition as a scholar, and effective medical education and/or clinical program administration. Substantial track record of investigation and scholarship, including peer-reviewed publications in high-impact journals of relevant specialty. Demonstrated capacity for leadership in an academic Internal Medicine department. Ability to serve as a role model for students and junior colleagues. Excellent communication and team-building skills Desirable Qualifications: Experience working in a multicultural environment, including understanding the unique cultural aspects of Hawaii’s population. Documented participation in the scholarly and academic and/or clinical affairs of the medical school, university, professional organizations, and/or hospitals. Recognition as an outstanding academician, scholar, or clinician with a national and/or international reputation. Successful acquisition of funding for clinical trials, clinical services, or educational training grants and/or contracts. Demonstrated ability to lead a research/scholarship group or Center, provide research/scholarship training for junior faculty and/or graduate students, and/or lead research studies involving clinical trials, community-based research, quality improvement projects, or clinical services and intervention. Senior departmental or division leadership in a GME program, clinical division, service line, clinical program, or academic department, with evidence of mentoring faculty. Managerial experience in healthcare administration, medical management, or equivalent. Experience in strategic planning leading to division or departmental growth To Apply: Click on the \"Apply\" button on the top right corner of the screen to complete an application and attach the required documents: a cover letter indicating how you satisfy the minimum and desirable qualifications, current curriculum vitae, Printout of your current American Board of Internal Medicine and any related subspecialty U.S. board certification, names of five (5) professional references (complete with contact information, including e-mail address). The application will be considered incomplete if any required documents are missing or unreadable.  Incomplete applications will not be considered.  Note: If you have not applied for a position before using NEOGOV, you will need to create an account. Inquiries: Dr. Thomas Read, Chair, Department of Surgery tread6@hawaii.edu EEO, Clery Act, ADA The University of Hawai'i is an Equal Opportunity Institution and is committed to a policy of nondiscrimination in employment, including on the basis of veteran and disability status.  For more information, visit: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/policies/ Employment is contingent on satisfying employment eligibility verification requirements of the Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986; reference checks of previous employers; and for certain positions, criminal history record checks. In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, annual campus crime statistics for the University of Hawai'i may be viewed at: https://www.hawaii.edu/titleix/help/campus-security/ , or a paper copy may be obtained upon request from the respective UH Campus Security or Administrative Services Office. Accommodation Request: The University of Hawai'i complies with the provisions of the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). Applicants requiring a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process should contact the EEO coordinator directly. Determination on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis. For further information, please refer to the following link: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/accommodation-request/ Employer University of Hawaii Department University of Hawai'i at Manoa - John A. Burns School of Medicine Address 651 Ilalo Street Honolulu, Hawaii, 96813 Website http://workatuh.hawaii.edu Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Career Opportunities at the University of Hawai'i Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026