    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/hawaiiedu/jobs/5352111/assistant-associate-professor-md6-course-director-0088902t-readvertisement": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor (MD6 Course Director, 0088902T) READVERTISEMENT",
      "description": "Career Opportunities at the University of Hawai'i | University of Hawai'i For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Assistant/Associate Professor (MD6 Course Director, 0088902T) READVERTISEMENT | University of Hawai'i page has loaded. Assistant/Associate Professor (MD6 Course Director, 0088902T) READVERTISEMENT | University of Hawai'i page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Career Opportunities at the University of Hawai'i Menu Career Opportunities at the University of Hawai'i Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. University of Hawai'i powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Assistant/Associate Professor (MD6 Course Director, 0088902T) READVERTISEMENT Print Apply ﻿ Assistant/Associate Professor (MD6 Course Director, 0088902T) READVERTISEMENT Salary Depends on Qualifications Location UH Manoa - JABSOM, Kaka'ako - Honolulu, HI Job Type Part-Time Temporary Job Number 2026-01062 Department University of Hawai'i at Manoa - John A. Burns School of Medicine Division Associate Dean for Academic Affairs Opening Date 06/29/2026 Closing Date Continuous Position Number: 0088902T Description Title: Assistant/Associate Professor (MD6 Course Director) Position Number: 0088902T Hiring Unit: John A. Burns School of Medicine – Office of Medical Education Location:  John A Burns School of Medicine, Medical Education Building Date Posted: 6/29/2026 Closing Date:  Continuous, First review on 7/14/2026 Salary Information: Salary commensurate with qualifications and experience. Monthly Type: 11 Month Tenure Track: Non-Tenure Full Time/Part Time: Part Time - Full Time Equivalency: 25% Temporary/Permanent: Temporary Other Conditions: To begin approximately July 2026 subject to position clearance and availability of funds. Position is renewable subject to performance and/or funding availability. Duties & Responsibilities: Serve as one of the co-course directors for the MD6 (Neuro/Locomotor/Behavioral) curricular unit. Plan and implement the contents and activities for the course, including PBL case development and modification. Appropriately assess student performance and provide necessary student remediation. Ensure that all aspects of the course are in-line with JABSOM's educational philosophy and advance students towards achievement of the JABSOM graduation objectives. Recruit, orient, and facilitate evaluation of PBL tutors. Participate as a member of the JABSOM pre-clinical education committee. Maintain and update the curriculum map and content maps related to the course. Recruit speakers for course lectures/seminars/workshops, work with OME staff to schedule sessions and communicate with speakers, and help to facilitate speaker evaluations. Assign tasks to supervise and evaluate Junior Course Directors assigned to their course. Facilitate PBL sessions as a tutor in at least one MD unit during the academic year. Contributes to the mission of the Office of Medical Education in the areas of faculty development, community service, and community outreach. Contributes to the preparation for LCME accreditation. Attend and participate in functions required of all OME faculty, such as Medical Education Grand Rounds, Faculty Meetings, and Convocation. Participate or lead educational task forces under the Office of Medical Education, the Curriculum Committee, or another educational subcommittee. Provide lectures or conferences/colloquia upon request. Evidence of effective teaching is required. This includes evidence of facilitating student-centered learning and demonstration of a positive attitude to student growth. Serve on JABSOM and/or University committees. Conduct scholarly work in medical education which may include research or curriculum descriptions. The scholarly work should be published and/or presented at peer-reviewed forums. Other duties as assigned (includes but not limited to participating in community engagement activities, directing office initiatives, etc.) Minimum Qualifications: Assistant Professor: M.D. or D.O. degree or equivalent medical degree from an accredited medical school. Relevant board certification in or qualification in the clinical discipline of the specific position. Demonstrated clinical and/or educational expertise in one or more of the following areas: neurology, musculoskeletal/sports medicine, or psychiatry Professionalism in meeting and conferring with others Excellent organizational skills Evidence of effective teaching Demonstrated potential for research/scholarship Experience using teaching methods such as problem-based learning, team-based learning, project-based learning, or another method that emphasizes active, self-directed learning Associate Professor: Same as Assistant Plus... In the rank of Assistant Professor, or four years of other health care experience, or a total of four years of teaching in the rank of Assistant Professor and other experience, or on year at the rank of Associate Professor at another health care school of recognized .standing . Proven ability in teaching, research, and program administration. Recognition for having made a significant scholarly contribution to the clinical specialty. Ability to serve as a role model for students and junior colleagues. Professionalism in meeting and conferring with others. Desirable Qualifications Three (3) years of experience in medical student education Teaching evaluations that attest to creative and innovative teaching methods that are well-received by students Demonstrated ability to work and teach collaboratively with other faculty within and across disciplines Comfortable working in a multi-cultural setting To Apply: Applicants must submit the following electronically via Work at UH: cover letter indicating how you satisfy the minimum and desirable qualifications; current Curriculum Vitae; names and contact information of five (5) professional references, and official transcripts or original documentation from the institution confirming degree or copy of U.S. board certification or U.S. medical license (copies of transcripts are accepted when used in lieu of current U.S. board certification or current U.S. medical license, however, if used for verification, original transcripts sent directly from the degree granting institution is required upon hire). Incomplete applications will not be reviewed. Inquiries: Maria Uyeunten - monsell@hawaii.edu EEO, Clery Act, ADA The University of Hawai'i is an Equal Opportunity Institution and is committed to a policy of nondiscrimination in employment, including on the basis of veteran and disability status.  For more information, visit: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/policies/ Employment is contingent on satisfying employment eligibility verification requirements of the Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986; reference checks of previous employers; and for certain positions, criminal history record checks. In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, annual campus crime statistics for the University of Hawai'i may be viewed at: https://www.hawaii.edu/titleix/help/campus- security/, or a paper copy may be obtained upon request from the respective UH Campus Security or Administrative Services Office. Accommodation Request: The University of Hawai'i complies with the provisions of the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). Applicants requiring a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process should contact the EEO coordinator directly. Determination on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case- by-case basis. For further information, please refer to the following link: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/accommodation-request/ Employer University of Hawaii Department University of Hawai'i at Manoa - John A. Burns School of Medicine Address 651 Ilalo Street Honolulu, Hawaii, 96813 Website http://workatuh.hawaii.edu Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Career Opportunities at the University of Hawai'i Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this setting does not apply, however, you can review your right on our privacy policy . If you require further assistance, please email privacy@neogov.com × Accessibility Statement At Governmentjobs.com, Inc. d/b/a NEOGOV, we recognize the importance of making our products\n                    and services accessible to all individuals, including those with disabilities, and are continually\n                    working to improve the experience for all 