      "title": "Associate Dean for Research (#0089508)",
      "description": "Career Opportunities at the University of Hawai'i | University of Hawai'i For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Associate Dean for Research (#0089508) | University of Hawai'i page has loaded. Associate Dean for Research (#0089508) | University of Hawai'i page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Career Opportunities at the University of Hawai'i Menu Career Opportunities at the University of Hawai'i Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. University of Hawai'i powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Associate Dean for Research (#0089508) Print Apply ﻿ Associate Dean for Research (#0089508) Salary See Position Description Location UH Manoa - JABSOM, Kaka'ako - Honolulu, HI Job Type Full-Time Permanent Job Number 2026-01075 Department University of Hawai'i at Manoa - John A. Burns School of Medicine Opening Date 05/22/2026 Closing Date Continuous Position Number: 0089508 Description Title: Associate Dean for Research Position Number: 89508 Hiring Unit: Coll of Hlth Sci & SW, School of Medicine, Associate Dean for Research Location: Kaka’ako, Honolulu, HI Date Posted: May 22, 2026 Closing Date:  Continuous Recruitment. First review of applications will begin on June 15, 2026 and will continue until position is filled. Salary Range:  $162,156 to $291,885 Annual Additional Salary Info: Commensurate with qualifications and experience Full Time/Part Time:  Full-time Temporary/Permanent:  Permanent Funding: General Funds Other Conditions: Position to begin approximately September 2026. INTRODUCTION The primary objective of the Associate Dean for Research is to assist the Dean in managing the research operations for the John A. Burns School of Medicine (JABSOM). This position also oversees the JABSOM Graduate Programs and serves as a liaison with the Dean of the Graduate Division. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Assists the Dean in the overall day-to-day administration of JABSOM research operations, including working on the Dean's behalf to oversee all functional areas of the school's research and infrastructure administration relating to planning, policy development, and program supervision for graduate programs. Under the direction of the Dean, ensures compliance with all state, federal, and university rules and regulations related to research conducted at the John A. Burns School of Medicine (JABSOM). Develops and implements policies and procedures for research at JABSOM to facilitate the conduct of sound, safe research in learning and working environ ments that comply with state, federal, and NIH-specific expectations . Ensures that the mission, vision, and goals of JABSOM are met to maintain the highest-quality research and teaching. Fosters an environment where excellence in research enhances the mission of the school, campus, and university. Provides a strategic foundation for the JABSOM research mission in developing scientific discovery and prioritizing translational research to transform findings into clinical applications. Develops and implements formal guidance and support mechanisms to assist faculty with individual research programs. Develops and coordinates resources to facilitate scholarly achievement of faculty and students. Develops and maintains continuous quality improvement programs for the school's research mission . Enhances the function of the JABSOM grants application and management offices in conjunction with the Institutional Review Board (IRB), Office of Research Services (ORS), and other entities at the UH System level, including Data Governance and Data Security . Serves as a liaison between clinical research training, clinical outcomes assessment, clinical research networks, and translational research by working closely with the Chief Academic Officers of JABSOM-affiliated healthcare systems, the infrastructure grant leads that support clinical research, and the UHCC Clinical Trials Office. Collaborates with Kaka ? ako Campus Chief Financial Officer (CFO) to develop and manage the research operating budget of the school. Oversees administrative and fiscal responsibilities for JABSOM research infrastructure, ensuring sound fiscal management and compliance with regulations for grants and contracts. Assists the Dean with oversight of research support faculty and staff. May maintain own research program as evidenced by publications and research grants. Collaborates directly with the UH Manoa Dean of Graduate Division to provide comprehensive oversight of all JABSOM graduate programs (i.e. , Master's , PhD, graduate certificates), ensuring academic excellence and a safe learning and working environment. Supports advising for JABSOM graduate students. Participates in UHM and UH System research meetings (i.e., those convened by the Office of the Vice-President for Research and Innovation) Assists Center/Institute Directors in the development and implementation of developing and implementing strategic plans for research centers/institutes in collaboration with other UH campus and community entities. Assists the JABSOM Dean with fundraising for research, including working with hospital system leadership to provide academic mission support for strategically-focused strategically focused research programs. Assists with research linkages within the UH system and into the Pacific, as well as between JABSOM and institutions on the U.S. Continent. Helps the JABSOM Dean sustain focused research themes at the school that resonate with the community or our collective strengths (especially in support of JABSOM research infrastructure grants). Develops and maintains the cross-disciplinary and cross-school relationships required to increase the research visibility and productivity of JABSOM, the campus, and the university. Maintains a network of research relationships at the state, national, and international levels. Adheres to applicable laws, regulations, and policies and procedures of the University, raises awareness among staff, and directs them in such a way that University compliance requirements are met. Identifies and mitigates through policy development/revision/enhancement and training, areas of risk and developing risk to the University, e.g., legal, financial, reputation, and compliance risk, and ensures team is aware and focused on addressing same. All other duties as assigned by the dean. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Doctorate (e.g., PhD or MD) from an accredited college or university. Five (5) years of professional experience working in administrative management at an accredited medical school or equivalent research leadership experience. Such experience shall include overseeing complex research operations in compliance with university rules and state and federal laws, facilitating resources for faculty and students, and collaborating (specifically, as Principal Investigator) with other principal investigators and researchers on a diverse portfolio of extramurally funded projects. Demonstrated knowledge of the principles and practices of research operations in an accredited medical school; knowledge of the policies and practices involved in the administration of a medical school. Demonstrated knowledge of working with unionized faculty in higher education. Ability to comprehend and interpret administrative directives and guidance to ensure IT operations align with organizational standards and industry best practices. Ability to communicate effectively, both orally and in writing. Strong interpersonal skills with the ability to cultivate collaborative relationships, solve problems, think creatively, and resolve conflicts. DESIRABLE QUALIFICATIONS In addition to PhD or MD degree, either possess an MBA, MPH, JD, or Med. TO APPLY: Click on the \"Apply\" button on the top right corner of the screen to complete an application and attach required documents. Applicant must submit the following: Cover letter indicating how you satisfy the minimum and desirable qualifications CV Names and contact information of five professional references Official transcripts (or original documentation from the institution confirming degree or copy of U.S. board certification or U.S. medical license). Copies of transcripts are accepted when used in lieu of current U.S. board certification or current U.S. medical license, however, if used for verification, original transcripts are required upon hire. The application will be considered incomplete if materials are unreadable. Late or incomplete applications will not be considered. INQUIRIES: Email: hrkccas@hawaii.edu EEO, Clery Act, ADA The University of Hawai'i is an Equal Opportunity Institution and is committed to a policy of nondiscrimination in employment, including on the basis of veteran and disability status.  For more information, visit: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/policies/ Employment is contingent on satisfying employment eligibility verification requirements of the Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986; reference checks of previous employers; and for certain positions, criminal history record checks. In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, annual campus crime statistics for the University of Hawai'i may be viewed at: https://www.hawaii.edu/titleix/help/campus-security/ , or a paper copy may be obtained upon request from the respective UH Campus Security or Administrative Services Office. Accommodation Request: The University of Hawai'i complies with the provisions of the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). Applicants requiring a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process should contact the EEO coordinator directly. Determination on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis. For further information, please refer to the following link: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/accommodation-request/ Employer University of Hawaii Department University of Hawai'i at Manoa - John A. Burns School of Medicine Address 651 Ilalo Street Honolulu, Hawaii, 96813 Website http://workatuh.hawaii.edu Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Career Opportunities at the University of Hawai'i Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this setting does not apply, however, you can review your right on our privacy policy . If you require further assistance, please email privacy@neogov.com × Accessibility Statement At Governmentjobs.com, Inc. d/b/a NEOGOV, we recognize the importance of making our products\n                    